      "timestamp": "2024-04-02T04:17:10.315+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": "2024-04-02T04:26:08.167+00:00",
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "This is a sort of a Proof of Concept of a Zine-style for UTEP. It takes one concept, \"Agency\", and tries to incorporate that into different ideas/essays. Agency is a very dear concept to my heart, and that concept cannot be simply explored with one lens. As such, I've written 3 different essays on Agency that explore different aspects that I've learned about. The first focuses on Linux and Religion, The second focuses on Programming and Writing, and the third focuses on Concordat and Community. These are deliberately diverse, as the goal above all else is to explore: how does our different disciplines and realities clash and inform one another?\n\nIn the future, I'd like to have some artworks, poems, stories and the like that can explore future concepts as well. We are never bound to one medium for expression, and I'd like to feature as many of them as I can. Well, I'll see public interest first before I go any further.\n\nFor now, I sincerely hope you enjoy the zeroth publication of the zine, \"Explication\".\n\n- Halley\n\n*TABLE OF CONTENTS*\n1. Linux: A Religious Perspective - Halley\nhttps://forum.theeastpacific.com/t/linux-a-religious-perspective/17926/1\n2. Writing as a programmer - Halley\nhttps://forum.theeastpacific.com/t/writing-as-a-programmer/17927/1\n3. Concordat: Crystallization of Community - Halley\nhttps://forum.theeastpacific.com/t/concordat-crystallization-of-community/17928/1",
